Software Requirements Specification (SRS)

 ## TYRF Turf Booking & Discovery Platform

 **Version:** 1.1\
 **Target Market:** Nairobi, Kenya\
 **Application Type:** Mobile-first responsive web application\
 **Future Module:** 3D Turf Map & Navigation

---

 # 1\. Introduction

 ## 1.1 Purpose

 TYRF is a web-based platform for discovering, booking, and managing football turfs in Nairobi.

 The system will allow customers to search for turfs, view availability, reserve time slots, make payments, and manage their bookings.

 Turf owners will be able to manage venues, pitches, availability, pricing, bookings, and revenue through an owner dashboard.

 Administrators will manage users, venues, bookings, payments, disputes, and platform operations.

 A future version of TYRF will introduce an interactive **3D Turf Map & Navigation subsystem**, allowing users to explore football venues through a simplified 3D representation of roads, turfs, entrances, landmarks, and navigation routes.

---

 # 2\. Product Vision

 TYRF aims to become a digital platform for discovering and accessing football facilities.

 The initial product focuses on:

 > **Find → Check availability → Book → Pay → Play**

 The long-term vision expands this into:

 > **Discover → Explore → Navigate → Book → Play**

 The 3D map is therefore considered a future differentiation layer rather than a dependency of the core booking system.

