 # 18\. Future Module — TYRF 3D Map & Navigation

 ## 18.1 Overview

 The 3D Map & Navigation subsystem will provide an interactive visual representation of football venues and their surrounding environment.

 The purpose is not to reproduce an entire 3D version of Nairobi.

 Instead, TYRF will create a **purpose-built football-oriented geographic environment**.

 The system may represent:

 - Roads.
- Terrain.
- Turf locations.
- Turf boundaries.
- Venue buildings.
- Entrances.
- Parking.
- Relevant landmarks.
- Walking paths.
- Navigation routes.

---

 # 19\. 3D Map Objectives

 The future subsystem shall allow users to:

 - Explore nearby turfs visually.
- Select a turf directly from the 3D map.
- View venue information.
- View turf availability.
- Navigate to a venue.
- Identify the correct venue entrance.
- Identify parking/access points where available.
- Transition from map exploration to booking.

 Example:

```
3D MAP
   ↓
Select Turf
   ↓
Venue Information
   ↓
Check Availability
   ↓
Book
   ↓
Get Directions
```

---

 # 20\. 3D Data Architecture

 The 3D subsystem shall be independent of the core booking engine.

 Example:

```
Turf
 ├── id
 ├── venue_id
 ├── latitude
 ├── longitude
 └── 3d_model_id

3D Venue
 ├── model_id
 ├── turf_id
 ├── entrance
 ├── parking
 └── navigation metadata
```

 This allows the booking platform to function even if a venue does not yet have a 3D model.

 ## 20.1 Progressive Modelling

 Venues should have different representation levels:

 ### Level 1 — Location

 Simple turf marker.

 ### Level 2 — Simplified Model

 Basic 3D representation of the venue/turf.

 ### Level 3 — Detailed Model

 Detailed venue, entrance, parking and surrounding environment.

 This allows TYRF to scale the 3D system gradually.

---

 # 21\. 3D Map MVP for Future Phase

 The first 3D prototype should not attempt to model all of Nairobi.

 A pilot area should be selected with a limited number of venues.

 The prototype should include:

 - Basic terrain.
- Roads.
- Selected turf locations.
- Simple 3D turf models.
- Venue entrances.
- Basic navigation.
- Turf selection.
- Link to booking.

 The objective is to validate whether the 3D experience improves turf discovery and navigation before investing in large-scale modelling.

