**One architectural decision I'd make now:** build **one responsive web application**, not separate mobile and desktop applications. Design it mobile-first, but let the same Next.js application progressively enhance itself for tablets and desktops. This gives TYRF a much lower initial development cost while keeping the door open for a future PWA or native mobile app.

 The next logical artifact is the **database ERD + complete PostgreSQL schema**, because that will turn this SRS from a product specification into an implementable technical specification.
